{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/1agpxl","slideIndex":2,"text":"One project that brings these skills together is a cloud-based court case management system for debt recovery. It was designed to centralize case records and support the work around those cases. I developed the web application using Laravel, PHP and Filament, and worked on its cloud deployment using Oracle Cloud Infrastructure. The architecture keeps the application and database on separate virtual machines connected through a private network. Docker and GitHub Actions support repeatable deployment, and the system generates Sinhala-language PDF reports.\n\nThis project taught me to think beyond whether a feature works on my computer. Access control, deployment, database connectivity and document output all affect whether the system is useful in practice. A separate cloud-native lab is extending that learning through Kubernetes, infrastructure automation and monitoring.\n\nSource: https://lk.linkedin.com/in/charithkalhara"}
